 Length		 Length		 Pairs		 Time		  Time
--------	 ------		-------		------		--------
    625		   49		 15,025		   5.1		    13.1


  2,500		   99		122,550		  49		    91
								 (1:31)

 10,000		  199		990,100		 475		   705
					       (7:55)	        (11:45)

 40,000		  399	      7,960,200        5,390		 5,813
					    (1:29:50)	      (1:36:53)

 62,500		  499	     15,562,750       11,965		11,515
					    (3:19:25)	      (3:11:55)


  The following equations fit the observed (worst case) data well:

  Fast Time (in Seconds) = (/ (expt length 1.685) 10600)
  Hybrid Time		 = (/ (expt length 1.475) 1080)

Solving this pair of equations yields a cross-over length of 52,875
(or an alphabet size of 230.)  This corresponds to a running time of
8578 seconds (2:22:58).

The rate at which the (initially) slower Hybrid algorithm overcomes its
nearly 10X overhead deficit is with the 5-th root of sequence length.
